cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the article and this repository."
title: "EpiBit: cytosine-resolved information-theoretic analysis of the Linaria vulgaris Peloria epiallele"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and supporting data for the cytosine-level
  information-theoretic analysis of the Peloria epiallele of Linaria vulgaris.
  EpiBit converts targeted bisulfite sequencing reads into site-wise Shannon
  entropy, directional Kullback-Leibler divergence, Jensen-Shannon divergence,
  mean bidirectional divergence and cumulative divergence dimensionality.
  The repository is dual-licensed: code under the MIT License, data and tables
  under CC-BY 4.0. See the LICENSE file for the full terms.
